  "result": "I revised the node record for NRS_484B_363_4 and wrote it to `record.jsonl`. It hasn't been through the gate yet.\n\n**What I changed:** the `blind` scenario now masks `kin.position` instead of `rel.bearing`.\n- **Why the old mask failed:** when the source has no measured bearing, Core works out `rel.bearing` from both vehicles' `kin.position` and the subject's `kin.heading`. Masking `rel.bearing` only removes a measured value, so it changed nothing. That is why `blind` got the same result as `forbid`: violated.\n- **Why the new mask works:** without `kin.position`, Core can't compute the overtaking-pass concept, the bearing, the overlap along the subject's heading, or whether the subject is in the zone. So whether the duty applies becomes unknown, which is what `blind` expects.\n\n**Other edits:**\n- **Pass element (`s2`) and obligation:** these now say that the overtaking-pass concept reads both vehicles' positions and is unknown when they are missing.\n- **Assumptions:** the three `asm.*` assumptions reuse ids already in the catalogue, so I dropped their `meaning` text, as the rules require.\n\nEverything else in the record is unchanged. On the coder's diagnostic run, where the other vehicle's position was missing, the rule and the other 17 witnesses passed. That run didn't apply a mask, though, so the new `blind` still needs the gate to confirm it.",
